  "intro": "QuickBooks Online, FreshBooks, Xero, Zoho Books and Bonsai are five Wave alternatives, with entry prices running from $0 free plans to QuickBooks Simple Start at $38 per month. The right choice depends on whether you need a free tier, plans priced by client or invoice count, multi-user accounting, project and inventory tracking, or time tracking with proposals and contracts. At The Modern Wallet, we show the arithmetic behind accounting software so you can see what user fees, add-ons and payment rates total over a full year.\n\n[Wave](https://www.waveapps.com/) lists a Starter plan at $0 with unlimited invoices, estimates, bills and bookkeeping records, while charging 2.9% + $0.60 per credit card transaction and 3.4% + $0.60 per American Express (Amex) transaction. Wave Pro lists at $19 United States Dollars (USD) per month billed monthly or $190 USD per year, which is also listed at $25 Canadian Dollars (CAD) per month or $250 CAD per year. Wave Pro adds automatic bank transaction imports through Plaid, automated categorization, receipt capture and a 2.9% + $0 transaction fee on the first 10 credit card payments each month.\n\nFor other accounting and billing shortlists, see the [QuickBooks alternatives](/alternatives/quickbooks/) guide, the [FreshBooks alternatives](/alternatives/freshbooks/) comparison, and the [best accounting software for freelancers roundup](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/). Readers can also browse the [comparison hub](/compare/) for wider software breakdowns.",
